Package: qcom-va-driver
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: VA-API driver with an encoder for the Qualcomm iris video core (Diting)
 VA-API backend on Qualcomm Iris through the V4L2 stateful encoder and
 decoders, for the Xiaomi 12T Pro (diting): H.264 (Constrained Baseline,
 Main, High) and HEVC Main encoding in hardware, CQP, CBR or VBR, for
 VA-API applications.
 .
 Installed as qcom_drv_video.so and nothing else. A program selects it with
 LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=qcom; without that, it gets libva-v4l2-stateful, which
 keeps the msm and v4l2 driver names and decodes for the browsers.

Package: qcom-va-driver-tests
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Depends: qcom-va-driver (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Hardware tests of qcom-va-driver
 The tests of upstream qcom-va-driver, to run on the phone against its own
 video core: the encoder ones (api-smoke, async, ffmpeg-smoke.py) and the
 decoder ones. In /usr/libexec/qcom-va-driver/tests; they take the driver
 from LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=qcom.
